IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 3, SUBPART 1, DRAFTING AND PUBLISHING LEGISLATION (ss 67 to 83A).
-- The Parliamentary Counsel Office (PCO) and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel are named in the Act; their staffing is not encoded.
-- What a person can take from this subpart: when legislation is published, what an official version proves, what is not part of the text, and what a court must notice.
-- s 83A (the annual report on exemptions) is encoded as a duty of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel and of the Attorney-General with the open-textured "as soon as practicable" taken as an input.

§ `Section 67 -- What legislation is drafted by PCO`

DECLARE `Thing to be drafted` IS ONE OF
    `Government Bills and amendments to them`
    `a Government Bill`
    `an amendment to a Government Bill`
    `local Bills and private Bills and amendments to them (to advise on or assist with)`
    `a local Bill`
    `a private Bill`
    `an amendment to a local Bill or a private Bill`
    `an amendment to a local Bill`
    `an amendment to a private Bill`
    `Members' Bills and amendments to them`
    `a Members' Bill`
    `an amendment to a Members' Bill`
    `secondary legislation made by Order in Council`
    `secondary legislation that amends an Act`
    `other secondary legislation`
    `any other legislation`

-- src:461 | 67 What legislation is drafted by PCO
-- src:462 | The main functions of the PCO, in relation to drafting legislation, are—
-- src:463 | to draft Government Bills and amendments to them; and
-- src:464 | to advise on, or assist with, the drafting of local Bills and private Bills and amendments to them; and
-- src:465 | to draft Members’ Bills, and amendments to them, if the Attorney-General directs; and
-- src:466 | to draft the following:
-- src:467 | any secondary legislation made by Order in Council (unless the Attorney-General otherwise directs):
-- src:468 | any secondary legislation that amends an Act:
-- src:469 | any secondary legislation if the administering agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree:
-- src:470 | any secondary legislation if the Attorney-General directs; and
-- src:471 | to draft, or advise on or assist in the drafting of, any other legislation that the Attorney-General directs.
-- The main functions of the PCO in relation to drafting legislation are to draft Government Bills; to advise on or assist with local and private Bills; to draft Members' Bills if the Attorney-General directs; to draft
-- secondary legislation made by Order in Council (unless the Attorney-General otherwise directs), secondary legislation that amends an Act, other secondary legislation if the administering agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree,
-- or if the Attorney-General directs; and to draft, or advise on or assist in the drafting of, any other legislation that the Attorney-General directs.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 67 (src:461) (src:462-471)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing to be drafted`
      `the Attorney-General directs it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administering agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a main drafting function of the PCO` thing `when` `the Attorney-General directs it` `or the Attorney-General otherwise directs:` `the Attorney-General otherwise directs` `or the agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree:` `the administering agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `Government Bills and amendments to them` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Government Bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an amendment to a Government Bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `local Bills and private Bills and amendments to them (to advise on or assist with)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a local Bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a private Bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an amendment to a local Bill or a private Bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an amendment to a local Bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an amendment to a private Bill` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Members' Bills and amendments to them` THEN `the Attorney-General directs it`
    WHEN `a Members' Bill` THEN `the Attorney-General directs it`
    WHEN `an amendment to a Members' Bill` THEN `the Attorney-General directs it`
    WHEN `secondary legislation made by Order in Council` THEN NOT `the Attorney-General otherwise directs`
    WHEN `secondary legislation that amends an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `other secondary legislation` THEN `the administering agency and the Chief Parliamentary Counsel agree` OR `the Attorney-General directs it`
    WHEN `any other legislation` THEN `the Attorney-General directs it`

§ `Section 68 -- Power to authorise IRD to draft Inland Revenue Bills`

-- src:472 | 68 Power to authorise IRD to draft Inland Revenue Bills
-- src:473 | The Governor-General may, by Order in Council made on the recommendation of the Attorney-General, authorise the Inland Revenue Department to draft Inland Revenue Bills that the responsible Minister directs.
-- src:474 | The Order in Council may state exceptions to the authorisation.
-- src:475 | The Order in Council is secondary legislation (see this Part for publication requirements).
-- src:476 | In this section,—
-- src:477 | Inland Revenue Bills means Bills, or parts of Bills, intended to become Acts, or parts of Acts, administered by the Inland Revenue Department
-- src:478 | responsible Minister means the Minister of the Crown who is responsible for the Inland Revenue Department.
-- The Governor-General may, by Order in Council made on the recommendation of the Attorney-General, authorise the Inland Revenue Department to draft Inland Revenue Bills that the responsible Minister directs.
-- The Order in Council may state exceptions to the authorisation. The Order in Council is secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 68(1) to (3) (src:472) (src:473-475) (src:478)
GIVEN `an Order in Council has been made on the recommendation of the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Bill is an Inland Revenue Bill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the responsible Minister directs the Inland Revenue Department to draft it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Order in Council states an exception that covers the Bill` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Inland Revenue Department is authorised to draft the Bill` `an Order in Council has been made on the recommendation of the Attorney-General` `the Bill is an Inland Revenue Bill` `the responsible Minister directs the Inland Revenue Department to draft it` `the Order in Council states an exception that covers the Bill` MEANS
        `an Order in Council has been made on the recommendation of the Attorney-General`
    AND `the Bill is an Inland Revenue Bill`
    AND `the responsible Minister directs the Inland Revenue Department to draft it`
    AND (NOT `the Order in Council states an exception that covers the Bill`)

@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 68(3) (src:475)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Order in Council authorising the Inland Revenue Department to draft Bills is secondary legislation` MEANS TRUE

§ `Section 69 -- PCO must publish all legislation`

DECLARE `Thing the PCO publishes` IS ONE OF
    `an introduced Bill`
    `an amendment to a Bill`
    `an Act`
    `secondary legislation drafted by the PCO`
    `minimum legislative information for secondary legislation drafted by the PCO`
    `secondary legislation not drafted by the PCO`

-- src:481 | The PCO must publish—
-- src:482 | all introduced Bills (and those amendments to Bills that the Attorney-General directs); and
-- src:483 | all Acts; and
-- src:484 | all secondary legislation drafted by the PCO; and
-- src:485 | minimum legislative information for all secondary legislation drafted by the PCO.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): s 69(1) lists the PCO's duties, so what is not on the list is not a duty this subsection gives: JUST FALSE. The PCO may still publish secondary legislation it did not draft, but only under s 69(3), which is a liberty.
-- src:480 | 69 PCO must publish all legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 69(1) (src:480) (src:481-485)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing the PCO publishes`
      `the Attorney-General directs that the amendment be published` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the PCO must publish` thing `when` `the Attorney-General directs that the amendment be published` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `an introduced Bill` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an amendment to a Bill` THEN JUST `the Attorney-General directs that the amendment be published`
    WHEN `an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `minimum legislative information for secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `secondary legislation not drafted by the PCO` THEN JUST FALSE

-- (2) The PCO must also notify the making of that secondary legislation by publishing the information required by regulations in the Gazette.
-- src:486 | The PCO must also notify the making of that secondary legislation by publishing the information required by regulations in the Gazette.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 69(2) (src:486)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing the PCO publishes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO must notify the making in the Gazette of` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:487 | The PCO may also publish secondary legislation that was not drafted by the PCO as if it were drafted by the PCO. In that case,—
-- src:488 | subsections (1)﻿(d) and (2) apply; and
-- src:489 | section 71 (how and when legislation must be published by PCO) applies; and
-- src:490 | any obligation under any other legislation for the secondary legislation to be published or notified in the Gazette is treated as satisfied.
-- (3) The PCO may also publish secondary legislation that was not drafted by the PCO as if it were; then s 71 applies, and any obligation under other legislation for it to be published or notified in the Gazette is treated as satisfied.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 69(3) (src:487-490)
GIVEN `the PCO has published it as if drafted by the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation under other legislation is to publish or notify it in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an obligation under other legislation to publish or notify the secondary legislation in the Gazette is treated as satisfied` `the PCO has published it as if drafted by the PCO` `the obligation under other legislation is to publish or notify it in the Gazette` MEANS
    `the PCO has published it as if drafted by the PCO` AND `the obligation under other legislation is to publish or notify it in the Gazette`

§ `Section 70 -- PCO must publish consolidations of legislation that is amended`

-- src:492 | The PCO must publish consolidations of—
-- src:493 | all Acts that are amended; and
-- src:494 | all secondary legislation drafted by the PCO that is amended.
-- The PCO must publish consolidations of all Acts that are amended and all secondary legislation drafted by the PCO that is amended.
-- src:491 | 70 PCO must publish consolidations of legislation that is amended
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 70(1) (src:491) (src:492-494)
GIVEN `it is an Act that is amended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is secondary legislation drafted by the PCO that is amended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO must publish a consolidation` `it is an Act that is amended` `it is secondary legislation drafted by the PCO that is amended` MEANS
    `it is an Act that is amended` OR `it is secondary legislation drafted by the PCO that is amended`

-- (2) A consolidation must incorporate the amendments made so that it shows the law as at its stated date. (3) It may also show the law as it would be amended by amendments that have not yet commenced if it clearly indicates that.
-- src:495 | A consolidation must incorporate the amendments made to the legislation so that it shows the law as at its stated date.
-- src:496 | The consolidation may also show the law as it would be amended by amendments that have not yet commenced if it clearly indicates that those amendments have not yet commenced.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 70(2) and (3) (src:495-496)
GIVEN `it shows the law as it would be amended by amendments that have not yet commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it clearly indicates that those amendments have not yet commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a consolidation may show amendments that have not yet commenced` `it shows the law as it would be amended by amendments that have not yet commenced` `it clearly indicates that those amendments have not yet commenced` MEANS
    (NOT `it shows the law as it would be amended by amendments that have not yet commenced`) OR `it clearly indicates that those amendments have not yet commenced`

§ `Section 71 -- How and when PCO must publish legislation and consolidations of legislation`

DECLARE `Thing published electronically` IS ONE OF
    `Bills`
    `Amendments to Bills`
    `Acts`
    `Secondary legislation drafted by the PCO`
    `Minimum legislative information for secondary legislation drafted by the PCO`
    `Consolidations of Acts`
    `Consolidations of secondary legislation that is drafted by the PCO`

DECLARE `Event that starts the PCO's time to publish` IS ONE OF
    `they are introduced`
    `the amendments are released`
    `they are enacted`
    `the legislation is made`
    `the Acts are amended`
    `the legislation is amended`

-- src:497 | 71 How and when PCO must publish legislation and consolidations of legislation
-- src:498 | The PCO must electronically publish the following things at the following times:
-- src:499 | What is required to be published
-- src:500 | When it must be published
-- src:501 | Bills
-- src:502 | As soon as practicable after they are introduced
-- src:503 | Amendments to Bills
-- src:504 | As soon as practicable after the amendments are released
-- src:505 | Acts
-- src:506 | As soon as practicable after they are enacted
-- src:507 | Secondary legislation drafted by the PCO
-- src:508 | As soon as practicable after the legislation is made
-- src:509 | Minimum legislative information for secondary legislation drafted by the PCO
-- src:510 | As soon as practicable after the legislation is made
-- src:511 | Consolidations of Acts
-- src:512 | As soon as practicable after the Acts are amended
-- src:513 | Consolidations of secondary legislation that is drafted by the PCO
-- src:514 | As soon as practicable after the legislation is amended
-- The table: Bills, as soon as practicable after they are introduced; Amendments to Bills, after the amendments are released; Acts, after they are enacted; Secondary legislation drafted by the PCO, after the legislation is made;
-- Minimum legislative information, after the legislation is made; Consolidations of Acts, after the Acts are amended; Consolidations of secondary legislation, after the legislation is amended.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 71(1) (src:497) (src:498-514)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing published electronically`
GIVETH AN `Event that starts the PCO's time to publish`
`the event after which the PCO must publish electronically as soon as practicable` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `Bills` THEN `they are introduced`
    WHEN `Amendments to Bills` THEN `the amendments are released`
    WHEN `Acts` THEN `they are enacted`
    WHEN `Secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` THEN `the legislation is made`
    WHEN `Minimum legislative information for secondary legislation drafted by the PCO` THEN `the legislation is made`
    WHEN `Consolidations of Acts` THEN `the Acts are amended`
    WHEN `Consolidations of secondary legislation that is drafted by the PCO` THEN `the legislation is amended`

-- The text gives no number of days: "as soon as practicable" is the whole time limit. The latest day is therefore never stated: NOTHING (explicit not-covered value).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 71(1) (src:500-514)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing published electronically`
      `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the latest day for the PCO to publish electronically` thing `after the event on` `the day of the event` MEANS NOTHING

-- (2) The PCO may also publish those things in printed form. (3) Legislation or proposed legislation is sufficiently published for the purposes of this Act (for any period during which it is not practicable to publish electronically)
-- if it is only published and made available in the way set out in subsection (2). (4) Minimum legislative information is sufficiently published if the secondary legislation containing it is published by the PCO under this Act.
-- src:516 | Legislation or proposed legislation is sufficiently published for the purposes of this Act (for any period during which it is not practicable to publish it electronically) if it is only published and made available in the way set out in subsection (2).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 71(3) (src:516)
GIVEN `it is not practicable to publish it electronically for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published in printed form and made available in the way notified to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`legislation or proposed legislation is sufficiently published for the period` `it is not practicable to publish it electronically for the period` `it is published in printed form and made available in the way notified to the public` MEANS
    `it is not practicable to publish it electronically for the period` AND `it is published in printed form and made available in the way notified to the public`

-- src:517 | Minimum legislative information is sufficiently published for the purposes of this Act if the secondary legislation containing that information (as required at the time of its publication) is published by the PCO under this Act.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 71(4) (src:517)
GIVEN `the secondary legislation containing the information is published by the PCO under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`minimum legislative information is sufficiently published` `the secondary legislation containing the information is published by the PCO under this Act` MEANS
    `the secondary legislation containing the information is published by the PCO under this Act`

-- (2) The PCO may also publish those things in printed form and make them available in the way notified to the public. A liberty of the PCO: it binds no one to do anything.
-- src:515 | The PCO may also publish those things in printed form and make them available in the way notified to the public.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 71(2) (src:515)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO may also publish those things in printed form` MEANS TRUE

§ `Section 72 -- How and when electronic versions of legislation must be available on legislation website`

-- src:520 | as far as practicable, legislation published by the PCO under this Act (including official electronic versions of legislation published under section 78) is at all times able to be accessed at, or downloaded from, the legislation website free of charge; and
-- The PCO must ensure that, as far as practicable, legislation published by the PCO under this Act is at all times able to be accessed at, or downloaded from, the legislation website free of charge.
-- Ruling B (fork F11): the duty is the section's own and carries its own limits ("published by the PCO", "as far as practicable"), so a case outside them is JUST FALSE.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 72(1)(a) (src:520)
GIVEN `it is legislation published by the PCO under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person may access or download the legislation from the legislation website free of charge` `it is legislation published by the PCO under this Act` `access is practicable` MEANS
    IF `it is legislation published by the PCO under this Act` AND `access is practicable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (1)(b) The PCO must also ensure that the way the legislation is made available meets any minimum requirements set by the regulations made under this Act for how that must be done.
-- src:519 | The PCO must ensure that,—
-- src:521 | it meets any minimum requirements set by the regulations made under this Act for how that must be done.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 72(1)(b) (src:519) (src:521)
GIVEN `the legislation is, as far as practicable, at all times able to be accessed at or downloaded from the legislation website free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the way that is done meets any minimum requirements set by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO has met section 72(1)` `the legislation is, as far as practicable, at all times able to be accessed at or downloaded from the legislation website free of charge` `the way that is done meets any minimum requirements set by the regulations` MEANS
    `the legislation is, as far as practicable, at all times able to be accessed at or downloaded from the legislation website free of charge` AND `the way that is done meets any minimum requirements set by the regulations`

§ `Section 73 -- Maker must publish secondary legislation not published by PCO (if required)`

-- src:525 | The maker of the secondary legislation must comply with the applicable publication requirements (if any) for that secondary legislation.
-- src:526 | For the purpose of this Act and any other legislation, the secondary legislation is published under this Act when the maker first complies with the applicable publication requirements.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 73(2) and (3) (src:525-526)
GIVEN `the day the maker first complies with the applicable publication requirements` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day on which the secondary legislation is published under this Act` `the day the maker first complies with the applicable publication requirements` MEANS
    `the day the maker first complies with the applicable publication requirements`

-- (1) This section applies to secondary legislation that is not published by the PCO. (2) The maker must comply with the applicable publication requirements (if any).
-- src:524 | This section applies to secondary legislation that is not published by the PCO.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 73(1) (src:524)
GIVEN `the PCO publishes the secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 73 applies to the secondary legislation` `the PCO publishes the secondary legislation` MEANS
    (NOT `the PCO publishes the secondary legislation`)

-- src:525 | The maker of the secondary legislation must comply with the applicable publication requirements (if any) for that secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 73(2) (src:525)
GIVEN `there are applicable publication requirements for the secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maker has complied with them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the maker has done what section 73(2) requires` `there are applicable publication requirements for the secondary legislation` `the maker has complied with them` MEANS
    (NOT `there are applicable publication requirements for the secondary legislation`) OR `the maker has complied with them`

§ `Section 74 -- Applicable publication requirements for secondary legislation not published by PCO`

DECLARE `Source of applicable publication requirements` IS ONE OF
    `the minimum requirements under regulations made under this Act`
    `the requirements recorded and published by the PCO under clause 14 of Schedule 1`
    `the requirements that applied under an Act to the empowering provision immediately before this section came into force`
    `none`

-- src:528 | The applicable publication requirements for any secondary legislation not published by the PCO are the first of the following that applies to its empowering provision:
-- src:529 | the minimum requirements that apply under regulations made under this Act (if any):
-- src:530 | the requirements recorded and published by the PCO under clause 14 of Schedule 1 (if any):
-- src:531 | the 1 or more requirements to publish, notify, or otherwise make secondary legislation available (together with any exemptions or limits on those requirements) that applied under an Act to the empowering provision immediately before this section came into force (if any).
-- (1) The applicable publication requirements are the first of the following that applies to the empowering provision: (a) the minimum requirements under regulations made under this Act (if any); (b) the requirements recorded and
-- published by the PCO under clause 14 of Schedule 1 (if any); (c) the requirements that applied under an Act to the empowering provision immediately before this section came into force (if any).
-- src:527 | 74 Applicable publication requirements for secondary legislation not published by PCO
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 74(1) (src:527) (src:528-531)
GIVEN `regulations made under this Act set minimum requirements that apply to the empowering provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the PCO has recorded and published requirements under clause 14 of Schedule 1 for the empowering provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `requirements applied under an Act to the empowering provision immediately before this section came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Source of applicable publication requirements`
`the applicable publication requirements come from` `regulations made under this Act set minimum requirements that apply to the empowering provision` `the PCO has recorded and published requirements under clause 14 of Schedule 1 for the empowering provision` `requirements applied under an Act to the empowering provision immediately before this section came into force` MEANS
    IF `regulations made under this Act set minimum requirements that apply to the empowering provision`
    THEN `the minimum requirements under regulations made under this Act`
    ELSE IF `the PCO has recorded and published requirements under clause 14 of Schedule 1 for the empowering provision`
         THEN `the requirements recorded and published by the PCO under clause 14 of Schedule 1`
         ELSE IF `requirements applied under an Act to the empowering provision immediately before this section came into force`
              THEN `the requirements that applied under an Act to the empowering provision immediately before this section came into force`
              ELSE `none`

-- (2) In addition, if section 75 applies to the secondary legislation, the applicable publication requirements include those set out in that section.
-- src:532 | In addition, if section 75 applies to the secondary legislation, the applicable publication requirements include those set out in that section.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 74(2) (src:532)
GIVEN `section 75 applies to the secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the applicable publication requirements include those in section 75` `section 75 applies to the secondary legislation` MEANS
    `section 75 applies to the secondary legislation`

§ `Section 75 -- Additional applicable publication requirements for secondary legislation with international transparency obligations under CPTPP`

-- src:534 | This section applies to secondary legislation not published by the PCO that—
-- src:535 | is made by a Minister or a relevant central government entity (even if the Minister or entity is performing a statutorily independent function); and
-- src:536 | relates to international transparency obligations (because the publishing under this Part of copies of and links to the legislation would help meet those obligations).
-- (1) Applies to secondary legislation not published by the PCO that is made by a Minister or a relevant central government entity (even if performing a statutorily independent function) and relates to international transparency obligations.
-- src:533 | 75 Additional applicable publication requirements for secondary legislation with international transparency obligations under CPTPP
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 75(1) (src:533) (src:534-536)
GIVEN `it is not published by the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by a Minister or a relevant central government entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to international transparency obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 75 applies to the secondary legislation` `it is not published by the PCO` `it is made by a Minister or a relevant central government entity` `it relates to international transparency obligations` MEANS
    `it is not published by the PCO` AND `it is made by a Minister or a relevant central government entity` AND `it relates to international transparency obligations`

-- (2) The maker must ensure that (a) it is published on the maker's website as soon as practicable; (b) its details are in, or with, it as published; (c) it and its details are, as far as practicable, able to be accessed at, or downloaded from,
-- the maker's website; and (d) links to it are forwarded to the PCO for publication without delay.
DECLARE `Additional requirement on a maker` IS ONE OF
    `publish it on the maker's website as soon as practicable`
    `include its details in, or with, it as published on the maker's website`
    `make it and its details, as far as practicable, able to be accessed at, or downloaded from, the maker's website`
    `forward links to it to the PCO for publication without delay and in accordance with any applicable directions under section 76`

-- src:537 | The additional applicable publication requirements for secondary legislation with international transparency obligations are that the maker must ensure that—
-- src:541 | links to the secondary legislation are forwarded to the PCO for publication (without delay and in accordance with any applicable directions under section 76).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 75(2) (src:537-541)
GIVEN requirement IS AN `Additional requirement on a maker`
      `section 75 applies to the secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the maker must ensure this` requirement `when` `section 75 applies to the secondary legislation` MEANS
    `section 75 applies to the secondary legislation`

-- (3) Subsection (2)(b) is taken to be satisfied if the secondary legislation amends (without replacing wholly) principal secondary legislation; the details relate to the amendments it makes; and the details are in or with a consolidation of the principal secondary legislation that is published as required by subsection (2).
-- src:542 | Subsection (2)﻿(b) is taken to be satisfied if—
-- src:545 | the details are in or with a consolidation of the principal secondary legislation that is published as required by subsection (2).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 75(3) (src:542-545)
GIVEN `it amends, without replacing wholly, principal secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details relate to the amendments it makes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the details are in or with a consolidation of the principal secondary legislation published as required by section 75(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the requirement to include details is taken to be satisfied` `it amends, without replacing wholly, principal secondary legislation` `the details relate to the amendments it makes` `the details are in or with a consolidation of the principal secondary legislation published as required by section 75(2)` MEANS
        `it amends, without replacing wholly, principal secondary legislation`
    AND `the details relate to the amendments it makes`
    AND `the details are in or with a consolidation of the principal secondary legislation published as required by section 75(2)`

§ `Section 76 -- Chief Parliamentary Counsel must support international transparency obligations`

-- src:553 | The maker must, if required to do so in writing by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, republish a copy of the secondary legislation promptly on the maker’s website in a form that complies with section 75.
-- (3) The maker must, if required to do so in writing by the Chief Parliamentary Counsel, republish a copy of the secondary legislation promptly on the maker's website in a form that complies with section 75.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 76(3) (src:553)
GIVEN `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has required it in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is secondary legislation with international transparency obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the maker must republish a copy promptly on the maker's website in a form that complies with section 75` `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has required it in writing` `it is secondary legislation with international transparency obligations` MEANS
    `the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has required it in writing` AND `it is secondary legislation with international transparency obligations`

-- (1) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must ensure that, as soon as practicable, links forwarded to the PCO under section 75 are published electronically and, as far as practicable, able to be accessed at, or downloaded from, the legislation website.
-- "As soon as practicable" is open-textured, so whether it has been done in time is an input. A link that was not forwarded under section 75 is outside the duty, which is then met (nothing is owed).
-- src:547 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must ensure that, as soon as practicable, links forwarded to the PCO under section 75 are—
-- src:549 | as far as practicable, able to be accessed at, or downloaded from, the legislation website.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 76(1) (src:547-549)
GIVEN `the link was forwarded to the PCO under section 75` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been published electronically as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is, as far as practicable, able to be accessed at or downloaded from the legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has met section 76(1) for the link` `the link was forwarded to the PCO under section 75` `it has been published electronically as soon as practicable` `it is, as far as practicable, able to be accessed at or downloaded from the legislation website` MEANS
    (NOT `the link was forwarded to the PCO under section 75`)
    OR (`it has been published electronically as soon as practicable` AND `it is, as far as practicable, able to be accessed at or downloaded from the legislation website`)

-- (2) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must give all or any makers, and ensure there is or are in force for all secondary legislation with international transparency obligations, a direction or directions setting out, in general terms, the nature of their details and the nature of their links and the form and manner in which they must be forwarded.
-- src:550 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must give all or any makers, and ensure there is or are in force for all secondary legislation with international transparency obligations, a direction or directions setting out, in general terms,—
-- src:552 | the nature of their links and the form and manner in which they must be forwarded.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 76(2) (src:550-552)
GIVEN `the secondary legislation has international transparency obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction is in force for it setting out, in general terms, the nature of its details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction is in force for it setting out, in general terms, the nature of its links and the form and manner in which they must be forwarded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has met section 76(2) for the secondary legislation` `the secondary legislation has international transparency obligations` `a direction is in force for it setting out, in general terms, the nature of its details` `a direction is in force for it setting out, in general terms, the nature of its links and the form and manner in which they must be forwarded` MEANS
    (NOT `the secondary legislation has international transparency obligations`)
    OR (`a direction is in force for it setting out, in general terms, the nature of its details`
        AND `a direction is in force for it setting out, in general terms, the nature of its links and the form and manner in which they must be forwarded`)

-- (4) A direction under this section is secondary legislation.
-- src:554 | A direction under this section is secondary legislation (see this Part for publication requirements).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 76(4) (src:554)
GIVEN `it is a direction under section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a direction of the Chief Parliamentary Counsel is secondary legislation` `it is a direction under section 76` MEANS
    `it is a direction under section 76`

§ `Section 77 -- Definitions for purposes of international transparency obligations`

DECLARE `Kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020, including a departmental agency named in Part 2 of that schedule that is part of that department`
    `a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020`
    `a departmental agency named in Part 2 of that schedule that is part of that department`
    `an interdepartmental venture named in Part 4 of that schedule`
    `a Crown entity as defined in section 7(1) of the Crown Entities Act 2004`
    `a school board`
    `a tertiary education institution`
    `the Reserve Bank of New Zealand`
    `any other instrument of the Crown prescribed by regulations made under this Act`
    `a decision-making person or body in or related to, or acting through or for, any of the above`
    `any other body`

-- src:563 | relevant central government entity means any of the following (or a decision-making person or body in or related to, or acting through or for, any of the following):
-- src:564 | a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020, including any departmental agency named in Part 2 of that schedule that is part of that department:
-- src:565 | an interdepartmental venture named in Part 4 of that schedule:
-- src:566 | a Crown entity (as defined in section 7(1) of the Crown Entities Act 2004, but excluding a school board and a tertiary education institution):
-- src:567 | the Reserve Bank of New Zealand:
-- src:568 | any other instrument of the Crown prescribed, for the purposes of this paragraph, by regulations made under this Act (if any).
-- "relevant central government entity means any of the following (or a decision-making person or body in or related to, or acting through or for, any of the following): a department ...; an interdepartmental venture ...;
-- a Crown entity (as defined in section 7(1) of the Crown Entities Act 2004, but excluding a school board and a tertiary education institution); the Reserve Bank of New Zealand; any other instrument of the Crown prescribed ... by regulations (if any)."
-- Whether a body is one the Public Service Act 2020 or the Crown Entities Act 2004 names is a borrowed fact: the kind is the input.
-- "means any of the following" is a CLOSED list: a body that is off the list is not a relevant central government entity (JUST FALSE), where an "includes" list would leave it unsaid (NOTHING).
-- The first item prints a department and its departmental agency together, so the printed phrase and each of its two parts are members.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 77, definition of relevant central government entity (src:563-568)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a relevant central government entity` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020, including a departmental agency named in Part 2 of that schedule that is part of that department` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a department named in Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Public Service Act 2020` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a departmental agency named in Part 2 of that schedule that is part of that department` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an interdepartmental venture named in Part 4 of that schedule` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Crown entity as defined in section 7(1) of the Crown Entities Act 2004` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a school board` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a tertiary education institution` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the Reserve Bank of New Zealand` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other instrument of the Crown prescribed by regulations made under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a decision-making person or body in or related to, or acting through or for, any of the above` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `any other body` THEN JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Source of obligations` IS ONE OF
    `paragraph 5 of Article 26.2 (publication) of Chapter 26 of the Trans-Pacific Partnership Agreement done at Auckland on 4 February 2016`
    `that provision as incorporated into the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership by Article 1.1 of that agreement`
    `another obligation`

-- src:558 | international transparency obligations means obligations—
-- src:559 | under paragraph 5 of Article 26.2 (publication) of Chapter 26 (transparency and anti-corruption) of the Trans-Pacific Partnership Agreement done at Auckland on 4 February 2016; or
-- src:560 | under that provision as incorporated into the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership, done at Santiago, Chile, on 8 March 2018, by Article 1.1 of that agreement
-- "means obligations (a) ...; or (b) ..." is a CLOSED list: another obligation is not an international transparency obligation (JUST FALSE).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 77, definition of international transparency obligations (src:558-560)
GIVEN source IS A `Source of obligations`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`are international transparency obligations` source MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `paragraph 5 of Article 26.2 (publication) of Chapter 26 of the Trans-Pacific Partnership Agreement done at Auckland on 4 February 2016` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `that provision as incorporated into the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership by Article 1.1 of that agreement` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another obligation` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:562 | maker’s website means an Internet site (other than the legislation website) maintained by or on behalf of the maker
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 77, definition of maker's website (src:562)
GIVEN `it is an Internet site` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the legislation website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is maintained by or on behalf of the maker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is the maker's website` `it is an Internet site` `it is the legislation website` `it is maintained by or on behalf of the maker` MEANS
    `it is an Internet site` AND (NOT `it is the legislation website`) AND `it is maintained by or on behalf of the maker`

-- src:557 | details, for any secondary legislation at any time, means all information necessary or desirable for meeting, for that secondary legislation at that time, all applicable international transparency obligations
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 77, definition of details (src:557)
GIVEN `it is information necessary or desirable for meeting, for that secondary legislation at that time, all applicable international transparency obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a detail of the secondary legislation` `it is information necessary or desirable for meeting, for that secondary legislation at that time, all applicable international transparency obligations` MEANS
    `it is information necessary or desirable for meeting, for that secondary legislation at that time, all applicable international transparency obligations`

-- src:561 | links, in relation to any secondary legislation at any time, means all information necessary or desirable to enable a user at that time to access, using the legislation website, the secondary legislation as published and made available on the maker’s website
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 77, definition of links (src:561)
GIVEN `it is information necessary or desirable to enable a user at that time to access, using the legislation website, the secondary legislation as published and made available on the maker's website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a link in relation to the secondary legislation` `it is information necessary or desirable to enable a user at that time to access, using the legislation website, the secondary legislation as published and made available on the maker's website` MEANS
    `it is information necessary or desirable to enable a user at that time to access, using the legislation website, the secondary legislation as published and made available on the maker's website`

§ `Section 78 -- Official versions of legislation`

-- src:570 | 78 Official versions of legislation
-- src:571 | The PCO may publish—
-- src:572 | official electronic versions of legislation; and
-- src:573 | official printed versions of legislation.
-- src:574 | A printed version of legislation that is produced directly from an official electronic version is also an official version.
-- src:575 | An electronic or a printed document that is identified as an official version of legislation in accordance with regulations made under this Act must be treated as an official version unless the contrary is shown.
-- (1) The PCO may publish official electronic versions and official printed versions of legislation. (2) A printed version produced directly from an official electronic version is also an official version.
-- (3) An electronic or printed document identified as an official version in accordance with regulations made under this Act must be treated as an official version unless the contrary is shown.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 78 (src:570) (src:571-575)
GIVEN `the PCO published it as an official electronic or printed version` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a printed version produced directly from an official electronic version` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is identified as an official version in accordance with regulations made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an official version of legislation` `the PCO published it as an official electronic or printed version` `it is a printed version produced directly from an official electronic version` `it is identified as an official version in accordance with regulations made under this Act` `the contrary is shown` MEANS
        `the PCO published it as an official electronic or printed version`
    OR `it is a printed version produced directly from an official electronic version`
    OR (`it is identified as an official version in accordance with regulations made under this Act` AND (NOT `the contrary is shown`))

§ `Section 79 -- Legal status of official versions`

DECLARE `Kind of official version` IS ONE OF
    `an official version as originally enacted or made`
    `an official version that is a consolidation under section 70`
    `an official version that includes changes made under subpart 2`
    `an official version that is a consolidation and includes changes made under subpart 2`

DECLARE `What an official version is taken to prove` IS ONE OF
    `It is taken to correctly set out the text of the legislation`
    `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments`
    `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation and by the changes made, and is evidence that those changes are authorised by subpart 2`
    `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments (paragraph (b)) and by the changes made (paragraph (c)(i)), and is evidence that those changes are authorised by subpart 2`
    `The presumption does not apply: the contrary is shown`

-- src:576 | 79 Legal status of official versions
-- src:577 | An official version of legislation—
-- src:578 | (if it is as originally enacted or made) is taken to correctly set out the text of the legislation; and
-- src:579 | (if it is a consolidation under section 70) is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments; and
-- src:580 | (if it is a version of legislation that includes changes made under subpart 2)—
-- src:581 | is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation and by the changes made (and paragraph (b) also applies if the legislation is also a consolidation); and
-- src:582 | is evidence that those changes are authorised by that subpart.
-- src:583 | An official version of secondary legislation that states the date of publication by the PCO is evidence that the legislation was published on the date stated.
-- src:584 | The presumptions in this section apply unless the contrary is shown.
-- An official version of legislation (a) if as originally enacted or made, is taken to correctly set out the text of the legislation; (b) if a consolidation under section 70, is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated
-- and by the amendments; (c) if it includes changes made under subpart 2, is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation and by the changes made (and (b) also applies if it is also a consolidation), and is evidence that those changes are authorised by that subpart.
-- (3) The presumptions apply unless the contrary is shown.
-- A version that is BOTH a consolidation and includes subpart 2 changes gets paragraph (c)'s statement AND paragraph (b)'s ("paragraph (b) also applies if the legislation is also a consolidation"), so it has a result of its own, not the changes-only one.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 79(1) and (3) (src:576) (src:577-582) (src:584)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of official version`
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What an official version is taken to prove`
`what an official version of that kind is taken to prove` kind `unless the contrary is shown:` `the contrary is shown` MEANS
    IF `the contrary is shown`
    THEN `The presumption does not apply: the contrary is shown`
    ELSE CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `an official version as originally enacted or made` THEN `It is taken to correctly set out the text of the legislation`
         WHEN `an official version that is a consolidation under section 70` THEN `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments`
         WHEN `an official version that includes changes made under subpart 2` THEN `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation and by the changes made, and is evidence that those changes are authorised by subpart 2`
         WHEN `an official version that is a consolidation and includes changes made under subpart 2` THEN `It is taken to correctly state, as at its stated date, the law enacted or made by the legislation consolidated and by the amendments (paragraph (b)) and by the changes made (paragraph (c)(i)), and is evidence that those changes are authorised by subpart 2`

-- (2) An official version of secondary legislation that states the date of publication by the PCO is evidence that the legislation was published on the date stated.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 79(2) and (3) (src:583-584)
GIVEN `it is an official version of secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states the date of publication by the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an official version is evidence that the secondary legislation was published on the date stated` `it is an official version of secondary legislation` `it states the date of publication by the PCO` `the contrary is shown` MEANS
    `it is an official version of secondary legislation` AND `it states the date of publication by the PCO` AND (NOT `the contrary is shown`)

§ `Section 79A -- Legislative status of publication notes and information`

DECLARE `Item inserted by the PCO` IS ONE OF
    `machine-readable text, links or other metadata inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions`
    `machine-readable text inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions`
    `links inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions`
    `other metadata inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions`
    `a record of the legislative history of the legislation`
    `a record of the fact that changes have been made by the PCO under subpart 2`
    `information recorded and published under clause 14 of Schedule 1, or as an aid to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation`
    `information recorded and published under clause 14 of Schedule 1`
    `information published as an aid to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation`
    `another note or information`

-- src:585 | 79A Legislative status of publication notes and information
-- src:586 | The following, inserted by the PCO in carrying out its functions of publishing and consolidating legislation, do not form part of the text of the official version of legislation (even if published in that version):
-- src:587 | machine-readable text, links, or other metadata inserted as an aid to assist users of electronic versions of legislation:
-- src:588 | a record of the legislative history of the legislation (including a record of the fact that changes have been made by the PCO under subpart 2):
-- src:589 | information recorded and published by the PCO under clause 14 of Schedule 1 or as an aid to assist users to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation:
-- src:590 | any other note or information that is clearly identified, in a suitable place on the legislation website, as not forming part of the legislation.
-- The following, inserted by the PCO in carrying out its functions of publishing and consolidating legislation, do not form part of the text of the official version: (a) machine-readable text, links or other metadata; (b) a record of legislative history;
-- (c) information recorded and published under clause 14 of Schedule 1 or as an aid; (d) any other note or information that is clearly identified, in a suitable place on the legislation website, as not forming part of the legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 79A (src:585) (src:586-590)
GIVEN item IS AN `Item inserted by the PCO`
      `it is clearly identified, in a suitable place on the legislation website, as not forming part of the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an item inserted by the PCO forms part of the text of the official version` item `when` `it is clearly identified, in a suitable place on the legislation website, as not forming part of the legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `machine-readable text, links or other metadata inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `machine-readable text inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `links inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `other metadata inserted as an aid to users of electronic versions` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a record of the legislative history of the legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a record of the fact that changes have been made by the PCO under subpart 2` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `information recorded and published under clause 14 of Schedule 1, or as an aid to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `information recorded and published under clause 14 of Schedule 1` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `information published as an aid to understand how this Act applies to secondary legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another note or information` THEN
        IF `it is clearly identified, in a suitable place on the legislation website, as not forming part of the legislation`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 80 -- Evidential status of minimum legislative information`

DECLARE `Fact the minimum legislative information may evidence` IS ONE OF
    `that the secondary legislation was made`
    `that the secondary legislation was made on the date stated`
    `that the information was published on the date stated`
    `that the making of the secondary legislation was notified in the Gazette on the date stated`

-- src:593 | Publication of the minimum legislative information for secondary legislation is evidence of the following:
-- src:594 | that the secondary legislation was made; and
-- src:595 | if the date of making is stated, that the secondary legislation was made on that date; and
-- src:596 | if the date of publication of the information is stated with the information, that the information was published on the date stated; and
-- src:597 | if the date of notification of the making of the secondary legislation is stated in the Gazette, that the making of the secondary legislation was notified in the Gazette on the date stated.
-- src:598 | The presumptions in this section apply unless the contrary is shown.
-- Publication of the minimum legislative information for secondary legislation is evidence that it was made; if the date of making is stated, that it was made on that date; if the date of publication is stated with the information, that it was
-- published on that date; if the date of notification is stated in the Gazette, that the making was notified in the Gazette on that date. The presumptions apply unless the contrary is shown.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 80 (src:593-598)
GIVEN fact IS A `Fact the minimum legislative information may evidence`
      `the date is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`publication of the minimum legislative information is evidence` fact `if the date is stated:` `the date is stated` `unless the contrary is shown:` `the contrary is shown` MEANS
    (NOT `the contrary is shown`)
    AND CONSIDER fact
        WHEN `that the secondary legislation was made` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `that the secondary legislation was made on the date stated` THEN `the date is stated`
        WHEN `that the information was published on the date stated` THEN `the date is stated`
        WHEN `that the making of the secondary legislation was notified in the Gazette on the date stated` THEN `the date is stated`

-- (1) This section applies to minimum legislative information published under this Act.
-- src:592 | This section applies to minimum legislative information published under this Act.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 80(1) (src:592)
GIVEN `the information is minimum legislative information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 80 applies to the information` `the information is minimum legislative information` `it is published under this Act` MEANS
    `the information is minimum legislative information` AND `it is published under this Act`

§ `Section 81 -- Judicial notice of legislation`

-- src:599 | 81 Judicial notice of legislation
-- src:600 | All courts and persons acting judicially must take judicial notice of all legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 81 (src:599) (src:600)
GIVEN `it is a court or a person acting judicially` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`must take judicial notice` `it is a court or a person acting judicially` `of` `it is legislation` MEANS
    `it is a court or a person acting judicially` AND `it is legislation`

§ `Section 82 -- Power to revoke spent secondary legislation and other instruments`

-- src:603 | Before making a recommendation, the Attorney-General must be satisfied that the secondary legislation or other instrument has ceased to have effect or is no longer required.
-- (1) The Governor-General may, by Order in Council, on the recommendation of the Attorney-General, revoke any secondary legislation or other instrument. (2) Before making a recommendation, the Attorney-General must be satisfied that the secondary
-- legislation or other instrument has ceased to have effect or is no longer required. (3) This section is in addition to any other power to revoke. (4) An order under this section is secondary legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 82(2) (src:603)
GIVEN `the Attorney-General is satisfied that it has ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General is satisfied that it is no longer required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Attorney-General may recommend revocation under section 82` `the Attorney-General is satisfied that it has ceased to have effect` `the Attorney-General is satisfied that it is no longer required` MEANS
    `the Attorney-General is satisfied that it has ceased to have effect` OR `the Attorney-General is satisfied that it is no longer required`

-- src:605 | An order under this section is secondary legislation (see this Part for publication requirements).
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 82(4) (src:605)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an order under section 82 is secondary legislation` MEANS TRUE

-- (1) The Governor-General may, by Order in Council, on the recommendation of the Attorney-General, revoke any secondary legislation or other instrument. (3) This section is in addition to any other power to revoke.
-- src:602 | The Governor-General may, by Order in Council, on the recommendation of the Attorney-General, revoke any secondary legislation or other instrument.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 82(1) (src:602)
GIVEN `it is done by Order in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney-General has recommended it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Governor-General may revoke secondary legislation or another instrument under section 82` `it is done by Order in Council` `the Attorney-General has recommended it` MEANS
    `it is done by Order in Council` AND `the Attorney-General has recommended it`

-- src:604 | This section is in addition to any other power to revoke the secondary legislation or other instrument.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 82(3) (src:604)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 82 displaces any other power to revoke` MEANS FALSE

§ `Section 83 -- Attorney-General directions under this Part`

-- src:607 | 83 Attorney-General directions under this Part
-- src:608 | The PCO must carry out the functions in this Part subject to any directions by the Attorney-General—
-- src:609 | about the matters set out in section 67:
-- src:610 | consistent with this Act and regulations made under this Act, about—
-- src:611 | the form in which legislation or consolidations of legislation (or any class of them) must be published (including the omission of signatures and formal or introductory parts); and
-- src:612 | any other matters concerning the publication of legislation or proposed legislation or minimum legislative information.
-- src:613 | A direction given by the Attorney-General under this Part must be given to the PCO in writing.
-- The PCO must carry out the functions in this Part subject to any directions by the Attorney-General (a) about the matters set out in section 67; (b) consistent with this Act and regulations, about the form in which legislation or consolidations must be published
-- and any other matters concerning the publication of legislation or proposed legislation or minimum legislative information. A direction must be given to the PCO in writing.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 83 (src:607) (src:608-613)
GIVEN `the direction is about the matters set out in section 67` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction is about the form of publication or other publication matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the direction is consistent with this Act and regulations made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the PCO must carry out its functions subject to the direction` `the direction is about the matters set out in section 67` `the direction is about the form of publication or other publication matters` `the direction is consistent with this Act and regulations made under this Act` MEANS
        `the direction is about the matters set out in section 67`
    OR (`the direction is about the form of publication or other publication matters` AND `the direction is consistent with this Act and regulations made under this Act`)

@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 83(2) (src:613)
GIVEN `the direction is given to the PCO in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Attorney-General has given the direction as the Act requires` `the direction is given to the PCO in writing` MEANS
    `the direction is given to the PCO in writing`

§ `Section 83A -- Annual report on exemptions from presentation and other drafting and publication matters`

-- src:616 | The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must, as soon as practicable after the end of each financial year of the PCO, prepare a report on the following matters and provide it to the Attorney-General:
-- src:617 | the extent to which makers have relied on presentation exemptions during the previous financial year; and
-- src:618 | any other practices relating to the design, drafting, and publication of legislation that the Chief Parliamentary Counsel thinks fit.
-- (1) The Chief Parliamentary Counsel must, as soon as practicable after the end of each financial year of the PCO, prepare a report on the extent to which makers have relied on presentation exemptions during the previous financial year (and may add any other practices
-- relating to the design, drafting and publication of legislation that the Chief Parliamentary Counsel thinks fit) and provide it to the Attorney-General. (2) The Attorney-General must present the report to the House of Representatives.
-- "As soon as practicable" is an open-textured judgment and is taken as a plain input.
-- src:614 | Annual report on exemptions from presentation and other drafting and publication matters
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 83A(1) (src:614) (src:616-618)
GIVEN `the report on the extent to which makers relied on presentation exemptions during the previous financial year has been prepared` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been provided to the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was done as soon as practicable after the end of the financial year of the PCO` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Chief Parliamentary Counsel has met section 83A(1)` `the report on the extent to which makers relied on presentation exemptions during the previous financial year has been prepared` `it has been provided to the Attorney-General` `that was done as soon as practicable after the end of the financial year of the PCO` MEANS
        `the report on the extent to which makers relied on presentation exemptions during the previous financial year has been prepared`
    AND `it has been provided to the Attorney-General`
    AND `that was done as soon as practicable after the end of the financial year of the PCO`

-- src:619 | The Attorney-General must present the report to the House of Representatives.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 83A(2) (src:619)
GIVEN `the Attorney-General has presented the report to the House of Representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Attorney-General has met section 83A(2)` `the Attorney-General has presented the report to the House of Representatives` MEANS
    `the Attorney-General has presented the report to the House of Representatives`
